---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import { fetchGithubStars, formatStarCount } from "../github";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { GITHUB_URL } from "../site";

const stars = await fetchGithubStars();
const starsLabel = stars === null ? "Star" : formatStarCount(stars);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms · Rakazo"
  description="The terms for using Rakazo, including paid plans, cancellation, and refunds."
>
  <div class="container">
    <Header starsLabel={starsLabel} />
    <main id="main" class="privacy-copy">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p><strong>Last updated: October 7, 2026</strong></p>
      <p>
        These terms are an agreement between you and Inbox Zero Inc. (“Inbox Zero,” “we,” or “us”) for
        your use of the Rakazo service that we host, the Rakazo web, desktop, and mobile apps, and
        rakazo.com (together, the “Service”). By using the Service, you agree to these terms. If you
        use the Service on behalf of an organization, you confirm that you can bind that organization
        to these terms, and “you” includes it.
      </p>

      <h2>Open-source software</h2>
      <p>
        The Rakazo source code is available under the{" "}
        <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>Apache License 2.0</a>. That license, not these
        terms, governs your use of the code. It does not grant rights to the Rakazo name or logo; do
        not use them in a way that suggests we operate or endorse something we do not. A third party
        that operates a self-hosted Rakazo deployment is responsible for that deployment and its own
        terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <p>
        You must be at least 13 years old, and old enough to form a binding contract where you live,
        to use the Service. You may not use the Service if you are barred from doing so under US
        sanctions or export laws. Keep your sign-in details and connected credentials secure. You are
        responsible for activity in your account.
      </p>

      <h2>Bots and AI output</h2>
      <p>
        Bots act with the instructions, permissions, and connected accounts you give them, including
        when you are not watching, such as in scheduled routines. Actions your bots take, such as
        sending messages, changing data, making purchases, or running commands, are taken on your
        behalf and are your responsibility. Give bots only the access they need, and require approval
        for actions that are hard to undo.
      </p>
      <p>
        AI output can be inaccurate or incomplete. Review it before you rely on it. Do not use the
        Service where an error could cause death, injury, or serious harm, or to make decisions with
        legal, medical, or financial consequences for others without qualified human review.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You may not use the Service, or direct a bot, to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Break the law or infringe the rights of others.</li>
        <li>Send spam, distribute malware, or commit fraud.</li>
        <li>Access systems, accounts, or data you are not authorized to access.</li>
        <li>
          Interfere with the Service, circumvent its limits, or use its computers for cryptocurrency
          mining or attacks on other systems.
        </li>
        <li>Violate the terms of the model providers or connected apps you use through the Service.</li>
        <li>
          Create accounts by automated means or to evade limits, or resell or provide the hosted Service
          to others without our written permission.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>
        You keep ownership of the content you provide and the output your bots produce, and you are
        responsible for having the rights to provide it. You give us permission to host, process, and
        transmit that content only as needed to provide the Service, as described in our{" "}
        <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. We may use aggregated or de-identified
        usage data to operate and improve the Service. If you send us feedback, we may use it without
        obligation to you. Keep your own copies of content that matters to you.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        The Service can connect to model providers, voice and memory services, computer providers,
        and other apps you choose. Those services are governed by their own terms, and we are not
        responsible for them. You are responsible for fees they charge you, including usage your bots
        incur on your own API keys.
      </p>

      <h2>Paid plans and billing</h2>
      <p>
        Some features require a paid plan. Prices are shown before you subscribe. Subscriptions renew
        automatically at the end of each billing period until you cancel, and we charge the payment
        method on file, which is processed by Stripe. Prices exclude taxes unless stated otherwise.
        If your plan starts with a free trial, we collect a payment method at signup and charge it
        when the trial ends unless you cancel before then. Cancelling during the trial ends it, and you
        are not charged.
        Plans may include usage limits, and we may slow or pause usage that exceeds them or places an
        unreasonable load on the Service. If a payment fails, we may pause paid features until it
        succeeds. If you dispute a charge with your bank instead of contacting us, we may suspend the
        account while the dispute is open. We will notify you before a
        price change takes effect on your next renewal, and you can cancel before it does.
      </p>

      <h2>Cancellation and refunds</h2>
      <p>
        You can cancel at any time from your account’s billing settings or by emailing{" "}
        <a href="mailto:hello@rakazo.com">hello@rakazo.com</a>. Cancellation stops future renewals;
        you keep access until the end of the period you paid for. Payments are non-refundable and
        partial periods are not prorated, except where required by law. If you were charged in error,
        email us within 30 days and we will refund the charge.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are a consumer in the European Union or the United Kingdom, you can withdraw from a new
        subscription within 14 days of buying it by telling us, for example by email. Because you ask
        the Service to start immediately, we will refund your payment less an amount proportionate to
        the Service provided before you withdrew.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to the Service</h2>
      <p>
        We may add, change, or remove features. Features marked as beta or preview may be incomplete
        or change without notice, and we do not promise the Service will be uninterrupted or
        error-free. If we materially reduce a paid feature during your billing period, we will tell
        you in advance, and you can cancel and receive a refund for the unused period.
      </p>

      <h2>Termination</h2>
      <p>
        You can stop using the Service and delete your account at any time. We may suspend or
        terminate your access if you violate these terms, do not pay, or put the Service or others at
        risk, or if the law requires it. Where reasonable, we will tell you first. If we terminate
        your account or stop offering the Service for reasons other than a violation of these terms,
        we will give you reasonable notice and refund any prepaid fees for the unused period.
      </p>
      <p>
        When an account is deleted, its bots and routines stop and we delete its content as described
        in our privacy policy, so save anything you want to keep first. Terms that by their nature
        should survive termination, such as fees owed, disclaimers, limits of liability, and
        indemnity, continue to apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>
        TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED “AS IS” AND “AS AVAILABLE” WITHOUT
        WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, INCLUDING WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR
        PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, WE ARE NOT LIABLE FOR INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL,
        CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR FOR LOST PROFITS OR DATA. OUR TOTAL LIABILITY FOR ANY
        CLAIM RELATED TO THE SERVICE IS LIMITED TO THE GREATER OF THE AMOUNT YOU PAID US IN THE 12
        MONTHS BEFORE THE CLAIM OR US$100.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law, such as for fraud,
        gross negligence, or death or personal injury caused by negligence, or rights you have as a
        consumer that cannot be waived.
      </p>

      <h2>Indemnity</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent permitted by law, you will compensate us for third-party claims, and reasonable
        related costs, arising from your content, your bots’ actions, or your violation of these terms
        or the law.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. For material changes, we will notify you before they take effect.
        If you do not agree, you can cancel before then. Continuing to use the Service after that means
        you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>App stores</h2>
      <p>
        If you download a Rakazo app from an app store, that store’s terms also apply to the app. For
        the iOS app, Apple’s Standard EULA applies. Apple is not a party to these terms and is not
        responsible for the Service or its support.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Delaware, without regard to its conflict
        of law rules. Disputes will be resolved in the state or federal courts located in Delaware,
        except where your local law gives you the right to bring a claim where you live. To the extent
        permitted by law, you and we each waive any right to a jury trial.
      </p>

      <h2>General</h2>
      <p>
        These terms, together with any terms shown when you buy a plan, are the entire agreement
        between you and us about the Service. If any part is unenforceable, the rest stays in effect.
        Not enforcing a term is not a waiver. You may not transfer these terms without our consent; we
        may transfer them in connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets. Neither of us is
        responsible for delays caused by events beyond reasonable control. We may send you notices by
        email or in the Service, and you can send notices to us at the address below.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Inbox Zero Inc.<br />
        131 Continental Dr, Suite 305<br />
        Newark, Delaware 19713, United States<br />
        <a href="mailto:hello@rakazo.com">hello@rakazo.com</a>
      </p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
